{
  "id": "06113_kakemawaru",
  "headword": "{駆|か}け{回|まわ}る",
  "reading": "かけまわる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan, intransitive)",
  "gloss": "to run around; to rush about",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to run around; to rush about",
      "explanation": "To run around energetically in various directions, or to rush from place to place handling tasks."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06113_kakemawaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}たちが{庭|にわ}で{駆|か}け{回|まわ}っている。",
      "english": "The children are running around in the garden.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06113_kakemawaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{仕事|しごと}で{一日中|いちにちじゅう}{駆|か}け{回|まわ}っていた。",
      "english": "I was rushing around all day for work.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06113_kakemawaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{犬|いぬ}が{嬉|うれ}しそうに{駆|か}け{回|まわ}る。",
      "english": "The dog runs around happily.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMPOUND VERB:\n{駆|か}ける (to run, to gallop) + {回|まわ}る (to go around)\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n{自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive) - takes を for the area being covered or で for the location\n\nUSAGE:\nCan describe both playful running (like children or animals) and busy rushing between tasks.\n\nRELATED COMPOUND VERBS:\n- {走|はし}り{回|まわ}る: to run around (similar meaning, slightly more neutral)\n- {駆|か}け{上|あ}がる: to run up\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}む: to rush in",
